row(27, 'curved: equal-radius crossing cylinders (Steinmetz solid, keep; and cut)', ['x-cyl-cross-cyl-equal-keep', 'hg-cyl-perp-equal-cut'], 'refused', { raw: 'all', note: 'It BUILDS, and correctly: the keep returns after 245-346 s (round 1: 346.4 s; booleans-r2/raw-long: translator run 243.9 s, wall 493.4 s on the loaded box) at volume 2730.6369 against the closed form 16*8^3/3 = 2730.6667 and OCCT 2730.6667 (d 1.1e-5), but with 3 cylinder faces where OCCT has 4. The cut gave no result in 150 s. Both are refused up front by G2 because of the time, not the answer.', ops: CK, cat: ['curved'] });
row('27b', 'curved: a small cylinder with a perpendicular axis wholly inside a bigger one (surfaces never meet)', ['hg-cyl-inside-perp'], 'supported', { raw: 'all', note: 'Round 3 kept this as a false refusal; the round-4 nested-cylinder rule (W3) now lets it build, because a cylinder wholly inside the other never meets its surface. SECOND MEASURE, closed form: big cylinder r10 h40 = 12566.3706, small r2 h10 = 125.6637, so the cut leaves an internal void and 12440.7069 mm3; OCCT gives 12440.7069 and SolidCraft 12440.2979 (relative error 3.3e-5, inside the 3e-4 curved bar). The row is supported on that, not on OCCT alone.', ops: C, cat: ['curved'] });
row(28, 'curved: sphere with box and cylinder (box - sphere dimple, internal void, sphere - box, sphere + box, sphere & box, sphere with a bore through its centre)', ['x-sph-minus-box', 'x-box-minus-sph-hemi', 'x-box-minus-sph-void', 'x-box-minus-box-void', 'x-sph-union-box', 'x-sph-keep-box', 'x-sph-cut-cyl'], 'supported', { note: 'One sc.run takes 9-19 s CPU here: inside the 45 s budget, see the latency row.', ops: JCK, cat: ['curved'] });
row('29a', 'curved: sphere r15 with sphere r12 offset 10 (and 8 along x), union and cut: three extra cone-labelled faces', ['x-sph-union-sph', 'x-sph-cut-sph'], 'wrong', { raw: 'all', note: 'Volume, area, bbox and COM agree with OCCT (d 8e-5 / 5e-5) but SolidCraft reports 3 cone faces that OCCT does not have (OCCT: 2 sphere faces). booleans-r3/sphere-sphere-sweep.txt: the same pair gives the cones at offsets 8 and 10 along x and 2 cones along y, none at offset 12, and equal-radius balls of radius 10 give 2 sphere faces (row below); kernel faces are 14 in every case, so the "cone" labels are a face-grouping artefact that depends on where the intersection circle falls on the ball\'s six patches, not something a size rule can predict. No guard exists, so the row stays WRONG and is loud; downstream face picks on such a body are unmeasured.', ops: JC, cat: ['curved'] });
