row(35, 'coplanar faces (shared face, partial overlap, flush inside, identical operands, stacked, L shape, flush cut, coplanar caps, flush keep)', ['cop-union-shared-face', 'cop-union-partial-overlap', 'cop-union-inside-flush', 'cop-union-identical', 'cop-union-step', 'cop-union-l-shape', 'cop-cut-flush-top', 'cop-cut-caps', 'cop-cut-same-box', 'cop-keep-offset', 'cop-keep-partial'], 'supported', { ops: JCK, cat: ['coplanar'] });
row(36, 'tangent / touching contact that leaves one solid (cylinder overlapping 1 mm, internally tangent cylinders, cylinder stacked on a face, inscribed ball union / intersect, inscribed cylinder union, cylinder through a box tangent to ONE side, blind bore tangent to one side, ball through a box touching four sides at points); a later join or hole on a part cut by a cylinder tangent to ONE side', ['tan-union-cyl-overlap1', 'tan-cyl-in-cyl-internal', 'tan-union-cyl-on-face', 'tan-union-sph-inscribed', 'tan-keep-sph-inscribed', 'tan-union-cyl-inscribed', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-1', 'r3-tan-cyl-blind-1', 'r3-tan-sph-big', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-join', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-keep', 'r6-tan1-then-join', 'r6-tan1-then-hole'], 'supported', { solids: true, note: 'A cylinder through a box tangent to ONE side builds, matches OCCT (ONE solid each, the solid counts are asserted equal) and a later join or hole on it fuses and drills correctly (r6-tan1-then-*: area and volume equal OCCT). A ball touching four sides at points is one solid. Round 6: the two-adjacent-sides and two-opposite-sides cases left this row (next row): they come back as ONE body with TWO shells where OCCT has two solids, and the "one body, several shells" exception of the classifier had let them stand as supported.', ops: JCK, cat: ['tangent'] });
row('36c', 'a cylinder through a box tangent to TWO or THREE sides (two adjacent, two opposite, or three: box 40x40x20 with the cylinder r10 at 10,10; box 40x80x20 with r20; box 40x60x20 with r20 at y=10), at several sizes and positions', ['r3-tan-cyl-through-2', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-opp', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-3', 'r6-tan2-small', 'r6-tan2-large', 'r6-tan2-offset', 'r6-tan2-cone'], 'refused', { raw: 'differs', note: 'Round 6 (critic round 4, row 66): a cylinder through the part tangent to two sides separates a piece (a corner lump, or two halves) that touches the rest only along the tangent lines. SolidCraft returns ONE body with TWO shells where OCCT has two solids (r3-tan-cyl-through-2: faces 9 against 12, shells 2 and 2); the volume is right (5.5e-5 off the closed form), so the old classifier counted it supported under its \"one body, several shells\" exception. But the SAME body breaks the next step: a join onto the big lump leaves the contact interface as two unfused faces (area 2.7e-2 off OCCT, 3 shells, r6-tan2-then-join-big in the next row) while the volume stays right. Rule G7 now refuses a through-cylinder tangent to TWO or more sides (round 5: THREE and FOUR). Tangent to ONE side builds and stays supported (row {#36}). Round 3 had counted three tangent sides supported under the same exception (centre of mass 4.5e-5 against the 3e-5 bar, volume 1.5e-4 off). The cone case touches two sides at one point each: refused by the same rule. Unguarded, the numbers are on the lines below.', ops: C, cat: ['tangent'] });
row('36d', 'a join, hole or cut on a part that a cylinder tangent to two sides pinched (the critic repro: join a box onto the big lump, hole through the part, a second cut; two opposite sides, then a join)', ['r6-tan2-then-join-big', 'r6-tan2-then-join-far', 'r6-tan2-then-hole', 'r6-tan2-then-cut', 'r6-tanopp-then-join'], 'refused', { raw: 'differs', ung: 'all', note: 'The pinching cut is refused (previous row), so every later step is skipped in one sentence with no step names. UNGUARDED (executor only, the lines below, booleans-r6/r3raw is not needed: the as-shipped lines carry the numbers) the join builds with THREE shells and an area 2.7e-2 (two-sides) or 1.7e-2 (opposite sides) off OCCT while the volume is 5e-5 / 1e-4 off: the volume bar alone cannot see the unfused interface faces. A hole() on the pinched part passed WITHOUT the one-piece sentence (one body, two shells). The follow-on cases are listed so that no later step can reach the pinched part.', ops: JC, cat: ['tangent'] });
row('36b', 'cut with a tool that only touches the part (tangent subtract, edge-touch cut, sphere touching at a point, tool resting on a face, cylinder tangent outside a side): nothing would be removed', ['tan-subtract-touching', 'tan-cut-edge-touch', 'tan-cut-sph-point', 'r3-policy-cut-touch-face', 'r3-policy-cut-tangent-cyl'], 'refused', { raw: 'all', note: 'POLICY REFUSAL, NOT AN ENGINE LIMIT: truck, OCCT and brep-rs all build these and agree that the result is the part unchanged (volume 32000 / 8000 in the as-shipped lines below). The contract refuses them because a cut that removes nothing and looks accepted is what a shape written without at: produces (round 2 critic: this is a policy choice, so it is labelled as one). A page that prefers the engines\' behaviour can drop G4 and G4b; the row would then be supported with a no-op result.', ops: C, cat: ['tangent'] });
row(37, 'join of operands that meet only along a line, at an edge, at a vertex or at a point (cylinder tangent to a face, sphere on a face, two boxes sharing an edge or a corner)', ['tan-union-cyl-exact', 'tan-union-sph-point', 'tan-union-edge-touch', 'tan-union-vertex-touch'], 'refused', { raw: 'all', note: 'As shipped SolidCraft returns ONE body with 2 shells and the right volume (OCCT: 2 solids), brep-rs refuses, and a pinched shell is what breaks the next fillet or shell (the G6 reason that also refuses row {#34c}).', ops: J, cat: ['tangent'] });
row(38, 'cut whose round tool touches the part\'s sides along lines or at points: inscribed ball or cylinder, a cylinder through the box tangent to all FOUR sides (inscribed in its square cross-section), a ball or cylinder wholly inside touching one face', ['tan-cut-sph-inscribed', 'tan-cut-cyl-inscribed', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-4', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-4-small', 'r3-tan-cyl-through-x', 'r3-tan-sph-in-1', 'r3-tan-cyl-side-in-1'], 'refused', { raw: 'all', ung: 'all', note: 'Round 2 refused only tools wholly inside the part. The critic\'s repro cut(box 40x40x20, cylinder r20 h40) got through the guard: one body of 13 faces and volume 6869.97 where OCCT has 4 solids and 20 faces (r3-tan-cyl-through-4: volume d 4.0e-4 against the 3e-4 bar, faces 13 against 20, OCCT 4 solids; the same at half size and with the axis along x). G7 now refuses a cylinder tangent to all FOUR sides, and a tool wholly inside the part that touches ONE side (the kernel refuses those itself, with developer text). Tangent to one, two or three sides builds and matches, so those are NOT refused (row {#36}). The unpatched phase0 translator was not re-run for r3-tan-cyl-through-4-small (the SolidCraft pkg was lost in a machine reboot before it could be); its executor-only result is listed above. brep-rs refuses all seven (two different texts: "cannot boolean these two solids" and its own pinch sentence).', ops: C, cat: ['tangent'] });
